{"id": 1, "ok": true, "cmd": "stoke", "ucas": "xr(x: u8, y: u8) = (x | y) - (x & y)\nstoke xr steps 50000 restarts 2 seed 5", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "stoke", "model": "gt1030", "seed": 5, "steps": 50000, "restarts": 2, "cost_as_written": 3, "proposals": 100000, "verified": 4, "programs": [{"expression": "x xor y", "cost": 1, "verified": "every input enumerated", "proved": true}, {"expression": "(x | y) xor x & y", "cost": 1, "verified": "every input enumerated", "proved": true}, {"expression": "x & y xor (x | y)", "cost": 1, "verified": "every input enumerated", "proved": true}]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "stoke xr under gt1030: Metropolis-Hastings over programs of up to 8 instructions (add sub mul and or xor shl shr not neg),\n  2 chains of 50000 proposals, seed 5; xr as written costs 3\n  100000 proposals, 83309 accepted, 83110 at distance 0 on the 40 tests (0 counterexamples joined them), 4 verified\n  cost 1      x xor y\n      every input enumerated\n  cost 1      (x | y) xor x & y\n      every input enumerated\n  cost 1      x & y xor (x | y)\n      every input enumerated\n  -> 1 against 3 (-66.7%)\n"}
{"id": 2, "ok": true, "cmd": "define", "ucas": "pa(x: u32, y: u32) = (x + y) * (x + y)", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "define", "name": "pa", "params": [{"name": "x", "type": "u32"}, {"name": "y", "type": "u32"}], "body": "(x + y)*(x + y)", "signature": "pa(x: u32, y: u32)"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": ""}
{"id": 3, "ok": true, "cmd": "define", "ucas": "pb(x: u32, y: u32) = x * x + 2 * x * y + y * y", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "define", "name": "pb", "params": [{"name": "x", "type": "u32"}, {"name": "y", "type": "u32"}], "body": "x*x + 2x*y + y*y", "signature": "pb(x: u32, y: u32)"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": ""}
{"id": 4, "ok": true, "cmd": "pit", "ucas": "pit pa pb trials 2", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "pit", "seed": 1, "trials": 2, "degree": 2, "verdict": "equal_probably", "error_probability": 7.52316384526264e-37}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "proof": {"kind": "probabilistic", "text": "polynomials of total degree at most 2, equal at 2 random points mod 2^61 - 1: two that differ agree at one with probability at most 2/(2^61 - 1) = 8.67e-19 (Schwartz-Zippel), at all 2 with at most 7.52e-37"}, "files": [], "text": "pit pa pb: polynomial identity testing (Schwartz-Zippel), seed 1\n  pa has total degree at most 2, pb at most 2\n  polynomials of total degree at most 2, equal at 2 random points mod 2^61 - 1: two that differ agree at one with probability at most 2/(2^61 - 1) = 8.67e-19 (Schwartz-Zippel), at all 2 with at most 7.52e-37\n  -> equal as polynomials over the integers, except with probability at most 7.52e-37 (not a proof: a probabilistic answer)\n     in u32 they are then equal for every input: reduction mod 2^32 is a ring homomorphism\n"}
{"id": 5, "ok": true, "cmd": "equiv", "ucas": "equiv pa pb", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "equiv", "equal": true, "exhaustive": false, "mismatch_points": 0, "method": "sampled", "sat": {"result": "gave_up", "aig_nodes": 19200}, "identity_test": {"result": "equal_probably", "error_probability": 5.659799424266695e-73}}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "proof": {"kind": "numeric", "text": "sampled, not proved; SAT gave up on 19200 AIG nodes within its budget of 100000 conflicts or 2 s"}, "files": [], "text": "pa and pb are equal on the domain of pa (sampled, not proved; SAT gave up on 19200 AIG nodes within its budget of 100000 conflicts or 2 s)\n  polynomials of total degree at most 2, equal at 4 random points mod 2^61 - 1: two that differ agree at one with probability at most 2/(2^61 - 1) = 8.67e-19 (Schwartz-Zippel), at all 4 with at most 5.66e-73: equal over the integers except with that probability, and then for every input here (a probabilistic answer, not a proof)\n"}
{"id": 6, "ok": true, "cmd": "phash", "ucas": "days(m: u8 in 1..12) = match m { 2 => 28, 4 | 6 | 9 | 11 => 30, 1 | 3 | 5 | 7 | 8 | 10 | 12 => 31, _ => 0 }\nphash days", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "phash", "model": "gt1030", "seed": 1, "keys": 12, "cost_chain": 42.375, "hash": "x & 15", "slots": 16, "cost_lookup": 7.875, "rewritten": true, "body": "[0, 31, 28, 31, 30, 31, 30, 31, 31, 30, 31, 30, 31, 0, 0, 0][m & 15]", "defined": "days_ph"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "proof": {"kind": "exhaustive", "text": "every input enumerated"}, "files": [], "text": "phash days under gt1030: 12 keys, the compare chain costs 42.375; seed 1\n  13 hash functions tried: masks and shifts, (x K) >> s, ((x xor x >> a) K) >> s, and a displacement table, K drawn at random\n  injective on the 12 keys (each slot checked): h(x) = x & 15, a table of 16 slots\n  every value of m in 1..12 is a key: no key check is needed\n  the lookup costs 7.875\n  -> [0, 31, 28, 31, 30, 31, 30, 31, 31, 30, 31, 30, 31, 0, 0, 0][m & 15]\n     cost 7.875 against 42.375 (-81.4%); equal to the switch for every input: every input enumerated\n  defined days_ph\n"}
{"id": 7, "ok": true, "cmd": "cost", "ucas": "t(i: u32 in 0..32767, y: f32) = i < 16000 ? exp(y) * sqrt(y) : y\ncost t consecutive i", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "cost", "model": "gt1030", "total": 13, "operations": 5, "by_class": [{"class": "cmp", "count": 1, "each": 2.375, "cost": 2.375}, {"class": "select", "count": 1, "each": 1.625, "cost": 1.625}, {"class": "fmul", "count": 1, "each": 1, "cost": 1}, {"class": "fsqrt", "count": 1, "each": 4, "cost": 4}, {"class": "ftrans", "count": 1, "each": 4, "cost": 4}], "selects": [{"condition": "i < 16000", "select": 1.625, "uniform_branch": 6.25, "divergent_branch": 20.625, "uniform_condition": false, "expected_branch": 1.64453125, "p_true": 0.48828125, "p_split": 0, "lanes": "consecutive", "best": "select"}], "best_total": 13}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "cost of t under gt1030: 13 (5 operations, shared subterms counted once)\n  cmp              1 x 2.375 = 2.375\n  select           1 x 1.625 = 1.625\n  fmul             1 x 1     = 1\n  fsqrt            1 x 4     = 4\n  ftrans           1 x 4     = 4\n  ?: on i < 16000  (arms cost 9 and 0)\n      select: +1.625   uniform branch: +6.25   divergent branch: +20.625\n      expected branch: +1.64453   (1024 warps of 32 consecutive lanes, all counted: 0.4883 all true, 0.5117 all false, 0 split)\n      -> select (condition varies per invocation; mark parameters 'uniform' if it does not)\n  estimate with the best form per ?: : 13\n"}
